      "message": "\u003e value \u0026\u003d ~GENMASK(47, 12) | ~GENMASK(9, 0) is all-ones, so the host\u0027s Physical_Address [47:12] and Page_Size/Size [9:0] bits aren\u0027t cleared before the shadow BASER value is OR\u0027d in, letting a host partially redirect an ITS table base. Should be value \u0026\u003d ~(GENMASK(47, 12) | GENMASK(9, 0));\n\nDone.\n\n\u003e One caveat: that mask clears the PA correctly for 4KB/16KB tables, but for 64KB pages register bits [15:12] also carry PA[51:48], so if the shadow BASER can use 64KB pages the mask must widen to match. So this depends on the the page size this path programs, worth checking/\n\nPA[51:48] is mapped to GITS_BASER[15:12] and that falls into the `GENMASK_ULL(47, 12)`. So in this function we are good. The rest of the logic does not realy on `GITS_BASER` value to calculate the base physical address, so we also should be good.",
